== Asset Register
#figure(caption: "Asset Register", table(
  columns: 4,
  table.header([*No.*], [*Asset*], [*Description / Purpose*], [*Security Importance*]),

  [1.],
  [User Budget Data (Buckets and Transactions)],
  [Expense records, bucket names and resulting total balances.],
  [These information are the most critical of the application, which could be the target of attacks.],

  [2.],
  [User Identities & Tokens],
  [User accounts including metadata such as their assigned role as well as session tokens for users and systems.],
  [Compromised accounts or tokens can be used to perform unauthorzed operations such as modifying the balance of buckets.],

  [3.],
  [Exported Transcations / Files],
  [CSV-file generated by the export service containing all expenses of one bucket.],
  [Little less importance than the raw user data, as it is only being generated upon request and stored until it was downloaded.],

  [4.],
  [External File Generation Dependency],
  [Helper-package used by the export service to create CSV-files.],
  [Limited, as it can only insert data into the content which is being saved as a file.],
))

== STRIDE Threat Model
#figure(caption: "STRIDE Threat Model", table(
  columns: (16%, auto, 20%, auto),
  table.header([*STRIDE Category*], [*Threat / Attack Scenario*], [*Affected Asset*],  [*Impact*]),

  [Spoofing],
  [An attacker successfully forges a token to identify as another user, admin or system.],
  [JWT Tokens],
  [Possibly compromisation of all data of the affected user or even the entire system, in case an admin / system token gets forged.],

  [Tampering],
  [A user is able to add transactions to another users bucket.],
  [User Budget Data],
  [Integrity of the users / systems data is compromised, possibly invalidating the financial tracking.],

  [Repudiation],
  [An administrator deletes a bucket but the system lacks sufficient logs to uniquely identify the acting user.],
  [User Budget Data / Application Audit Trails],
  [Unable to investigate security incidents in form of malicious actors.],

  [Information \ Disclosure],
  [An attacker performs a supply chain attack through the export service dependency, sending all data to an external server during the export.],
  [User Budget Data / External File Generation Dependency],
  [Breach of confidentiality of users financial data.],

  [Denial of Service],
  [An attacker submits thousands of expenses or repeatedly requests massive transaction exports, resulting in a system overload.],
  [Resource Service / Export Service],
  [Reduced availability of the application.],

  [Elevation of Privilege],
  [An attacker is able to create an account with the administrator role assigned.],
  [User Authentication / User Budget Data],
  [Unauthorized access to user data, as the assigned admin role bypassed authorization checks.],
))

